# Agent Execution Pitfalls

This note records recurring execution mistake patterns discovered during real work.

Write generalized lessons, not one-off complaints. Each entry should explain the trigger, the broader failure class, and the better default behavior.

## Planning And Context Discipline

- Do not restart a continuing task with a broad repo sweep when `PLANS.md` already documents the active blocker.
- Do not compress active work so far that sources, locked decisions, or the resume point are lost after context compaction.
- Do not leave durable decisions only in chat; update `PLANS.md` before execution and handoff.
- Do not treat conservative execution as permission to downscope the user's requested outcome.
- Before asking the user, do a targeted read-only investigation unless the repo or local environment is unavailable.

## Tooling And Validation Hygiene

- Prefer the narrowest reproducer before broad reruns.
- Keep passing output out of the working context.

## Learning Loop

- Capture the repeated pattern, not just the latest symptom.
- If a lesson becomes a stable repo-wide rule, promote it to `docs/engineering/project_principles.md`.
- If an actionable follow-up emerges from a pitfall, record it in `docs/codex/TASKS_BACKLOG.md` and promote it to `PLANS.md` only when work starts.
- Do not turn a pitfall into backlog work unless it has an activation trigger and a next safe action.
